bexpCount k` — the comparator statement `exact_count_and_sat k` of OpenAI's family 378","+  (*The Exponential Time Hypothesis is False*, 2026-10-25), **restated as a `def` of a `Prop`,","+  never proved and never an axiom**: one fixed primitive multi-tape machine exactly counts the","+  satisfying assignments of every CNF of width `≤ k` on `n` variables, in the collection's","+  canonical encoding of bit length `L`, in time `≤ C (L + 1)^d · 2^(A · ρ(n))` with","+  `ρ(n) = n (log log(n + 16))² / √log(n + 16)`, visiting at most `S (L + 1)^e` tape cells at","+  every step. The body is the comparator's statement character for character (the binder","+  `hk : 2 ≤ k` becomes the hypothesis of `ExactCountAndSat`); the machine model, the encoding","+  and `runtimeBound` are the verbatim copy in `PrimitiveMachine.lean`. This is the *verified*","+  exponent, the weaker one (`reports/subexp_pathwidth.md` §1.0): the paper's","+  `n log log n / √log n` and `n / √log n` are not in the Lean library and are not restated.","+* `PathwidthSubexpOn C` — \"some primitive machine decides `pathwidth G ≤ k` for every graph","+  `G` in the class `C` and every `k`, in time `2^{o(n)} · poly(L)`\": a machine, constants","+  `c > 0`, `d`, and an exponent `f = o(n)` (`Asymptotics.IsLittleO`, so `2^(f n)` is","+  `2^{o(n)}` in the number of vertices), such that on the canonical input `encodeGraph G k`","+  (`n` and `k` in the collection's unary code, then the `n²` adjacency bits) the machine halts","+  in the answer state `decide (pathwidth G ≤ k)` within `c (L + 1)^d 2^(f n)` steps. A class is","+  `GraphClass := ∀ n, SimpleGraph (Fin n) → Prop` (the item's `SimpleGraph → Prop` is not a","+  type; nothing requires the class to be closed under isomorphism).","+* `PathwidthSubexp` — the same over every graph.","+","+The parameter is the number of vertices `n`, never the input length (`TASK.md`: on dense","+graphs `L = Θ(n²)`), which is why `f` is `o(n)` and the polynomial factor is in `L`.","+","+The machine model is the one the counting theorem is stated in, so a transfer theorem","+`SubexpCount k → PathwidthSubexpOn C` (item 09, if any) is a statement about one machine","+model and needs no translation between models; the price, recorded in the report, is that","+such a theorem needs a composition fact about primitive machines (a polynomial-time encoder","+followed by the counting machine), which the comparator does not state and which would be","+carried as a further named `Prop`. An abstract notion (\"a function with a time function\")","+was rejected because without a cost model `∃ f, ∃ T, …` is provable outright and the","+hypothesis would be vacuous.","+","+Proved here:","+","+* `SubexpCount.anti`: `SubexpCount k → k' ≤ k → SubexpCount k'` (a width-`≤ k'` formula has","+  width `≤ k`; the same machine and constants).","+* `PathwidthSubexpOn.mono`: a machine for a class is a machine for every subclass.","+* `pathwidthSubexp_iff`: `PathwidthSubexp ↔ PathwidthSubexpOn (fun _ _ => True)`.","+* `pathwidthSubexpOn_iff_vertexSeparation`: the same `Prop` with `vertexSeparation` in place","+  of `pathwidth` (Kinnersley, `vertexSeparation_eq_pathwidth`), for item 08, whose statements","+  are against `VertexSeparation.lean`.","+* `Trace.config_of_locatedStep`: a trace of the located (space-monitoring) step projects to a","+  trace of the plain step, so the time bound of `SubexpCount` is a bound on `machine.step`.","+* `runtimeScale_isLittleO`, `isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale`: the verified exponent","+  `A · ρ(n)` is `o(n)`, so `runtimeBound C A d L n` is of the form `PathwidthSubexpOn` asks","+  for (`runtimeBound_eq`). The analytic content is `(log y)² / √y → 0`.","+","+Every statement here is a definition or a trivial lemma; nothing was brute-force checked","+because nothing is a reduction or an encoding of pathwidth (TASK.md's check applies to those;","+`encodeGraph_length` is the one computation, proved). What this file does **not** claim:","+that `SubexpCount k` holds for any `k`; that any `PathwidthSubexpOn C` holds; that the","+`PrimitiveMachine` model is robust (polynomially equivalent to any other); or that the","+theorem of the paper beyond the comparator statement is restated.","+-/","+import MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.PrimitiveMachine","+import MOSPFormalization.VSEquivPW","+","+set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false","+","+namespace MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth","+","+open OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT","+open OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation","+open OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace","+open OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement","+open Asymptotics Filter","+","+/-! ### The hypothesis: the comparator statement as a `Prop` -/","+","+/-- **The counting hypothesis, for width `k`**: the body of `exact_count_and_sat k` in","+`lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.lean` of the OpenAI collection, character for","+character. Never proved here, never an axiom. -/","+def SubexpCount (k : ℕ) : Prop :=","+  ∃ (machine : Computation.PrimitiveMachine)","+    (countTape answerTape : Fin machine.tapeCount)","+    (C A S : ℝ) (d e : ℕ),","+    0 < C ∧ 0 < A ∧ 0 < S ∧ 0 < d ∧ 0 < e ∧","+    ∀ (n : ℕ) (F : SAT.CNF (Fin n)), SAT.WidthAtMost k F →","+      ∃ (time : ℕ) (final : LocatedCfg machine),","+        Computation.Trace (locatedStep machine) time","+          (locatedInit machine (Encoding.encodeCNF F)) final ∧","+        final.config.tapes countTape =","+          Turing.Tape.mk₁ ((countWord (SAT.count F)).map some) ∧","+        final.config.tapes answerTape =","+          Turing.Tape.mk₁ [some (decide (0 < SAT.count F))] ∧","+        final.config.state = Sum.inl (decide (0 < SAT.count F)) ∧","+        BinaryArithmetic.toNat (countWord (SAT.count F)) = SAT.count F ∧","+        (countWord (SAT.count F)).length ≤ n + 1 ∧","+        (time : ℝ) ≤ OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement.runtimeBound C A d","+          (Encoding.formulaBitLength F) n ∧","+        ∀ (prefixSteps : ℕ) (intermediate : LocatedCfg machine),","+          prefixSteps ≤ time →","+          Computation.Trace (locatedStep machine) prefixSteps","+            (locatedInit machine (Encoding.encodeCNF F)) intermediate →","+          (visitedSpace intermediate : ℝ) ≤","+            S * ((Encoding.formulaBitLength F : ℝ) + 1) ^ e","+","+/-- The comparator theorem in full: `SubexpCount k` for every `k ≥ 2`. A `Prop`, not asserted. -/","+def ExactCountAndSat : Prop := ∀ k : ℕ, 2 ≤ k → SubexpCount k","+","+/-- A machine for width `k` is a machine for every smaller width: `WidthAtMost k' F → WidthAtMost k F`. -/","+theorem SubexpCount.anti {k k' : ℕ} (h : SubexpCount k) (hk : k' ≤ k) : SubexpCount k' := by","+  obtain ⟨machine, countTape, answerTape, C, A, S, d, e, hC, hA, hS, hd, he, hmain⟩ := h","+  refine ⟨machine, countTape, answerTape, C, A, S, d, e, hC, hA, hS, hd, he, ?_⟩","+  intro n F hF","+  exact hmain n F (fun c hc => le_trans (hF c hc) hk)","+","+theorem ExactCountAndSat.subexpCount (h : ExactCountAndSat) {k : ℕ} (hk : 2 ≤ k) :","+    SubexpCount k := h k hk","+","+/-! ### The runtime bound is `2^{o(n)} · poly(L)` -/","+","+/-- An exponent `f` with `2^(f n) = 2^{o(n)}`: `f = o(n)` as `n → ∞`. -/","+def IsSubexpExponent (f : ℕ → ℝ) : Prop := f =o[atTop] (fun n : ℕ => (n : ℝ))","+","+/-- `runtimeBound C A d L n = C (L + 1)^d 2^(A · runtimeScale n)`, by definition. -/","+theorem runtimeBound_eq (C A : ℝ) (d L n : ℕ) :","+    runtimeBound C A d L n = C * ((L : ℝ) + 1) ^ d * (2 : ℝ) ^ (A * runtimeScale n) := rfl","+","+/-- `(log y)² / √y → 0` as `y → ∞`. -/","+theorem tendsto_log_sq_div_sqrt :","+    Tendsto (fun y : ℝ => (Real.log y) ^ 2 / Real.sqrt y) atTop (nhds 0) := by","+  have h := Real.isLittleO_log_rpow_rpow_atTop (2 : ℝ) (by norm_num : (0 : ℝ) < 1 / 2)","+  have h' : (fun y : ℝ => (Real.log y) ^ 2) =o[atTop] (fun y : ℝ => Real.sqrt y) := by","+    refine h.congr' ?_ ?_","+    · filter_upwards with y","+      exact Real.rpow_two _","+    · filter_upwards [eventually_ge_atTop (0 : ℝ)] with y hy","+      rw [Real.sqrt_eq_rpow]","+  exact h'.tendsto_div_nhds_zero","+","+/-- The verified runtime scale `ρ(n) = n (log log(n + 16))² / √log(n + 16)` is `o(n)`. -/","+theorem runtimeScale_isLittleO :","+    (fun n : ℕ => runtimeScale n) =o[atTop] (fun n : ℕ => (n : ℝ)) := by","+  have hlog : Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16)) atTop atTop :=","+    Real.tendsto_log_atTop.comp (tendsto_atTop_add_const_right _ _ tendsto_natCast_atTop_atTop)","+  have hq : Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => (Real.log (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))) ^ 2 /","+      Real.sqrt (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))) atTop (nhds 0) :=","+    tendsto_log_sq_div_sqrt.comp hlog","+  have h1 : (fun n : ℕ => (Real.log (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))) ^ 2 /","+      Real.sqrt (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))) =o[atTop] (fun _ : ℕ => (1 : ℝ)) :=","+    isLittleO_one_iff.mpr hq","+  have h2 := h1.mul_isBigO (isBigO_refl (fun n : ℕ => (n : ℝ)) atTop)","+  refine h2.congr' ?_ ?_","+  · filter_upwards with n","+    simp only [runtimeScale, Pi.mul_apply]","+    ring","+  · filter_upwards with n","+    simp","+","+/-- The verified exponent `A · ρ(n)` is a subexponential exponent, for every `A`. -/","+theorem isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale (A : ℝ) :","+    IsSubexpExponent (fun n : ℕ => A * runtimeScale n) :=","+  (runtimeScale_isLittleO.const_mul_left A)","+","+/-! ### Traces of the located step project to traces of the plain step -/","+","+theorem LocatedCfg.monitor_config {machine : PrimitiveMachine} (c : LocatedCfg machine)","+    (x : machine.Cfg) : (c.monitor x).config = x := by","+  unfold LocatedCfg.monitor","+  rcases hs : c.config.state with b | q","+  · rfl","+  · simp only [Sum.elim_inr]","+    rcases machine.transition q (c.config.tapes (machine.scan q)).head with b' | ⟨q', a⟩","+    · rfl","+    · rfl","+","+/-- A trace of the located step is a trace of the plain step on the configurations. -/","+theorem Trace.config_of_locatedStep {machine : PrimitiveMachine} {t : ℕ}","+    {c c' : LocatedCfg machine} (h : Trace (locatedStep machine) t c c') :","+    Trace machine.step t c.config c'.config := by","+  induction h with","+  | refl a => exact Trace.refl _","+  | cons hs _ ih =>","+    rename_i a b c''","+    simp only [locatedStep, Option.map_eq_some_iff] at hs","+    obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := hs","+    rw [LocatedCfg.monitor_config] at ih","+    exact Trace.cons hx ih","+","+/-! ### The canonical input of a pathwidth decision instance -/","+","+/-- The canonical input of the instance `(G, k)`, `G` a graph on `Fin n`: `n` in the","+collection's unary code (`encodeNat`), then `k`, then the `n²` adjacency bits row by row. -/","+noncomputable def encodeGraph {n : ℕ} (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ) : List Bool :=","+  open Classical in","+  Encoding.encodeNat n ++ Encoding.encodeNat k ++","+    (List.finRange n).flatMap (fun i => (List.finRange n).map (fun j => decide (G.Adj i j)))","+","+theorem encodeGraph_length {n : ℕ} (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ) :","+    (encodeGraph G k).length = (n + 1) + (k + 1) + n * n := by","+  simp [encodeGraph, Encoding.encodeNat, List.length_flatMap, List.map_const']","+","+/-! ### The subexponential-pathwidth predicates -/","+","+/-- A class of graphs, one predicate per vertex count. -/","+abbrev GraphClass := ∀ n : ℕ, SimpleGraph (Fin n) → Prop","+","+/-- `PathwidthSubexpOn C`: some primitive machine decides `pathwidth G ≤ k` for every `G` in","+the class `C` and every `k`, on the canonical input, in time `c (L + 1)^d 2^(f n)` with","+`f = o(n)` in the number of vertices `n`. -/","+def PathwidthSubexpOn (C : GraphClass) : Prop :=","+  ∃ (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (c : ℝ) (d : ℕ) (f : ℕ → ℝ),","+    0 < c ∧ IsSubexpExponent f ∧","+    ∀ (n : ℕ) (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ), C n G →","+      ∃ (time : ℕ) (final : machine.Cfg),","+        Trace machine.step time (machine.init (encodeGraph G k)) final ∧","+        final.state = Sum.inl (@decide (pathwidth G ≤ k) (Classical.propDecidable _)) ∧","+        (time : ℝ) ≤ c * (((encodeGraph G k).length : ℝ) + 1) ^ d * (2 : ℝ) ^ (f n)","+","+/-- `PathwidthSubexp`: the same over every graph. -/","+def PathwidthSubexp : Prop :=","+  ∃ (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (c : ℝ) (d : ℕ) (f : ℕ → ℝ),","+    0 < c ∧ IsSubexpExponent f ∧","+    ∀ (n : ℕ) (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ),","+      ∃ (time : ℕ) (final : machine.Cfg),","+        Trace machine.step time (machine.init (encodeGraph G k)) final ∧","+        final.state = Sum.inl (@decide (pathwidth G ≤ k) (Classical.propDecidable _)) ∧","+        (time : ℝ) ≤ c * (((encodeGraph G k).length : ℝ) + 1) ^ d * (2 : ℝ) ^ (f n)","+","+/-- Monotonicity in the class: a machine for `C` is a machine for every `C' ⊆ C`. -/","+theorem PathwidthSubexpOn.mono {C C' : GraphClass} (h : PathwidthSubexpOn C)","+    (hsub : ∀ n G, C' n G → C n G) : PathwidthSubexpOn C' := by","+  obtain ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, hmain⟩ := h","+  exact ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, fun n G k hG => hmain n G k (hsub n G hG)⟩","+","+/-- `PathwidthSubexp` is the class-restricted notion on the class of all graphs. -/","+theorem pathwidthSubexp_iff : PathwidthSubexp ↔ PathwidthSubexpOn (fun _ _ => True) := by","+  constructor","+  · rintro ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, hmain⟩","+    exact ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, fun n G k _ => hmain n G k⟩","+  · rintro ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, hmain⟩","+    exact ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, fun n G k => hmain n G k trivial⟩","+","+/-- The decision bit is the same for vertex separation (Kinnersley). -/","+theorem decide_pathwidth_le_eq {n : ℕ} (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ) :","+    @decide (pathwidth G ≤ k) (Classical.propDecidable _) =","+      @decide (vertexSeparation G ≤ k) (Classical.propDecidable _) := by","+  simp only [vertexSeparation_eq_pathwidth]","+","+/-- `PathwidthSubexpOn C`, stated with `vertexSeparation` in place of `pathwidth`, for the","+statements of item 08 that are made against `VertexSeparation.lean`. -/","+theorem pathwidthSubexpOn_iff_vertexSeparation (C : GraphClass) :","+    PathwidthSubexpOn C ↔","+    ∃ (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (c : ℝ) (d : ℕ) (f : ℕ → ℝ),","+      0 < c ∧ IsSubexpExponent f ∧","+      ∀ (n : ℕ) (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ), C n G →","+        ∃ (time : ℕ) (final : machine.Cfg),","+          Trace machine.step time (machine.init (encodeGraph G k)) final ∧","+          final.state = Sum.inl (@decide (vertexSeparation G ≤ k) (Classical.propDecidable _)) ∧","+          (time : ℝ) ≤ c * (((encodeGraph G k).length : ℝ) + 1) ^ d * (2 : ℝ) ^ (f n) := by","+  simp only [PathwidthSubexpOn, decide_pathwidth_le_eq]","+","+end MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/Ralph_Loops/loop0014/session_it02.jsonl","hunks":[{"oldStart":225,"oldLines":3,"newStart":225,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":221,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":178,\"session_id\":\"0ef12acb-f9ad-4899-992d-6d80c628ee09\",\"uuid\":\"a62ee91a-f33a-4c77-b222-cc7ca999517a\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5-1\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgiPE9QgzUBg832vePtQK\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"The copy compiles unchanged, and I'm writing Frame.lean with the hypothesis, the graph encoding, the subexponential predicates, and the bridging lemmas next.\\n\\n\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":32,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":487,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":126413,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":487,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"0ef12acb-f9ad-4899-992d-6d80c628ee09\",\"uuid\":\"369fdffc-93dd-43f1-9a1b-1d3b9ea8ac48\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T18:46:50.203Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgiPE91dKKSx7ETcKA2dB\",\"narration_block_indexes\":[0],\"thinking_duration_ms\":8,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5-1\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgiPE9QgzUBg832vePtQK\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01DdWLVtW6om46uKx69YQvzE\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cat > MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/Frame.lean <<'EOF'\\n/-\\nCopyright (c) 2026 Alexandre Linhares. All rights reserved.\\nReleased under the MIT license as described in the file LICENSE.\\n\\n# The formal frame of loop0014: `SubexpCount`, `PathwidthSubexp`, `PathwidthSubexpOn`\\n\\nItem 02 of `reports/subexp_pathwidth_plan.md` (§0.4.1, §0.5); `reports/subexp_pathwidth.md` §2.\\nEverything the loop proves about a subexponential exact algorithm for pathwidth is stated\\nagainst the three `Prop`s of this file:\\n\\n* `SubexpCount k` — the comparator statement `exact_count_and_sat k` of OpenAI's family 378\\n  (*The Exponential Time Hypothesis is False*, 2026-10-25), **restated as a `def` of a `Prop`,\\n  never proved and never an axiom**: one fixed primitive multi-tape machine exactly counts the\\n  satisfying assignments of every CNF of width `≤ k` on `n` variables, in the collection's\\n  canonical encoding of bit length `L`, in time `≤ C (L + 1)^d · 2^(A · ρ(n))` with\\n  `ρ(n) = n (log log(n + 16))² / √log(n + 16)`, visiting at most `S (L + 1)^e` tape cells at\\n  every step. The body is the comparator's statement character for character (the binder\\n  `hk : 2 ≤ k` becomes the hypothesis of `ExactCountAndSat`); the machine model, the encoding\\n  and `runtimeBound` are the verbatim copy in `PrimitiveMachine.lean`. This is the *verified*\\n  exponent, the weaker one (`reports/subexp_pathwidth.md` §1.0): the paper's\\n  `n log log n / √log n` and `n / √log n` are not in the Lean library and are not restated.\\n* `PathwidthSubexpOn C` — \\\"some primitive machine decides `pathwidth G ≤ k` for every graph\\n  `G` in the class `C` and every `k`, in time `2^{o(n)} · poly(L)`\\\": a machine, constants\\n  `c > 0`, `d`, and an exponent `f = o(n)` (`Asymptotics.IsLittleO`, so `2^(f n)` is\\n  `2^{o(n)}` in the number of vertices), such that on the canonical input `encodeGraph G k`\\n  (`n` and `k` in the collection's unary code, then the `n²` adjacency bits) the machine halts\\n  in the answer state `decide (pathwidth G ≤ k)` within `c (L + 1)^d 2^(f n)` steps. A class is\\n  `GraphClass := ∀ n, SimpleGraph (Fin n) → Prop` (the item's `SimpleGraph → Prop` is not a\\n  type; nothing requires the class to be closed under isomorphism).\\n* `PathwidthSubexp` — the same over every graph.\\n\\nThe parameter is the number of vertices `n`, never the input length (`TASK.md`: on dense\\ngraphs `L = Θ(n²)`), which is why `f` is `o(n)` and the polynomial factor is in `L`.\\n\\nThe machine model is the one the counting theorem is stated in, so a transfer theorem\\n`SubexpCount k → PathwidthSubexpOn C` (item 09, if any) is a statement about one machine\\nmodel and needs no translation between models; the price, recorded in the report, is that\\nsuch a theorem needs a composition fact about primitive machines (a polynomial-time encoder\\nfollowed by the counting machine), which the comparator does not state and which would be\\ncarried as a further named `Prop`. An abstract notion (\\\"a function with a time function\\\")\\nwas rejected because without a cost model `∃ f, ∃ T, …` is provable outright and the\\nhypothesis would be vacuous.\\n\\nProved here:\\n\\n* `SubexpCount.anti`: `SubexpCount k → k' ≤ k → SubexpCount k'` (a width-`≤ k'` formula has\\n  width `≤ k`; the same machine and constants).\\n* `PathwidthSubexpOn.mono`: a machine for a class is a machine for every subclass.\\n* `pathwidthSubexp_iff`: `PathwidthSubexp ↔ PathwidthSubexpOn (fun _ _ => True)`.\\n* `pathwidthSubexpOn_iff_vertexSeparation`: the same `Prop` with `vertexSeparation` in place\\n  of `pathwidth` (Kinnersley, `vertexSeparation_eq_pathwidth`), for item 08, whose statements\\n  are against `VertexSeparation.lean`.\\n* `Trace.config_of_locatedStep`: a trace of the located (space-monitoring) step projects to a\\n  trace of the plain step, so the time bound of `SubexpCount` is a bound on `machine.step`.\\n* `runtimeScale_isLittleO`, `isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale`: the verified exponent\\n  `A · ρ(n)` is `o(n)`, so `runtimeBound C A d L n` is of the form `PathwidthSubexpOn` asks\\n  for (`runtimeBound_eq`). The analytic content is `(log y)² / √y → 0`.\\n\\nEvery statement here is a definition or a trivial lemma; nothing was brute-force checked\\nbecause nothing is a reduction or an encoding of pathwidth (TASK.md's check applies to those;\\n`encodeGraph_length` is the one computation, proved). What this file does **not** claim:\\nthat `SubexpCount k` holds for any `k`; that any `PathwidthSubexpOn C` holds; that the\\n`PrimitiveMachine` model is robust (polynomially equivalent to any other); or that the\\ntheorem of the paper beyond the comparator statement is restated.\\n-/\\nimport MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.PrimitiveMachine\\nimport MOSPFormalization.VSEquivPW\\n\\nset_option linter.unusedSectionVars false\\n\\nnamespace MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth\\n\\nopen OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT\\nopen OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation\\nopen OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace\\nopen OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement\\nopen Asymptotics Filter\\n\\n/-! ### The hypothesis: the comparator statement as a `Prop` -/\\n\\n/-- **The counting hypothesis, for width `k`**: the body of `exact_count_and_sat k` in\\n`lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.lean` of the OpenAI collection, character for\\ncharacter. Never proved here, never an axiom. -/\\ndef SubexpCount (k : ℕ) : Prop :=\\n  ∃ (machine : Computation.PrimitiveMachine)\\n    (countTape answerTape : Fin machine.tapeCount)\\n    (C A S : ℝ) (d e : ℕ),\\n    0 < C ∧ 0 < A ∧ 0 < S ∧ 0 < d ∧ 0 < e ∧\\n    ∀ (n : ℕ) (F : SAT.CNF (Fin n)), SAT.WidthAtMost k F →\\n      ∃ (time : ℕ) (final : LocatedCfg machine),\\n        Computation.Trace (locatedStep machine) time\\n          (locatedInit machine (Encoding.encodeCNF F)) final ∧\\n        final.config.tapes countTape =\\n          Turing.Tape.mk₁ ((countWord (SAT.count F)).map some) ∧\\n        final.config.tapes answerTape =\\n          Turing.Tape.mk₁ [some (decide (0 < SAT.count F))] ∧\\n        final.config.state = Sum.inl (decide (0 < SAT.count F)) ∧\\n        BinaryArithmetic.toNat (countWord (SAT.count F)) = SAT.count F ∧\\n        (countWord (SAT.count F)).length ≤ n + 1 ∧\\n        (time : ℝ) ≤ OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement.runtimeBound C A d\\n          (Encoding.formulaBitLength F) n ∧\\n        ∀ (prefixSteps : ℕ) (intermediate : LocatedCfg machine),\\n          prefixSteps ≤ time →\\n          Computation.Trace (locatedStep machine) prefixSteps\\n            (locatedInit machine (Encoding.encodeCNF F)) intermediate →\\n          (visitedSpace intermediate : ℝ) ≤\\n            S * ((Encoding.formulaBitLength F : ℝ) + 1) ^ e\\n\\n/-- The comparator theorem in full: `SubexpCount k` for every `k ≥ 2`. A `Prop`, not asserted. -/\\ndef ExactCountAndSat : Prop := ∀ k : ℕ, 2 ≤ k → SubexpCount k\\n\\n/-- A machine for width `k` is a machine for every smaller width: `WidthAtMost k' F → WidthAtMost k F`. -/\\ntheorem SubexpCount.anti {k k' : ℕ} (h : SubexpCount k) (hk : k' ≤ k) : SubexpCount k' := by\\n  obtain ⟨machine, countTape, answerTape, C, A, S, d, e, hC, hA, hS, hd, he, hmain⟩ := h\\n  refine ⟨machine, countTape, answerTape, C, A, S, d, e, hC, hA, hS, hd, he, ?_⟩\\n  intro n F hF\\n  exact hmain n F (fun c hc => le_trans (hF c hc) hk)\\n\\ntheorem ExactCountAndSat.subexpCount (h : ExactCountAndSat) {k : ℕ} (hk : 2 ≤ k) :\\n    SubexpCount k := h k hk\\n\\n/-! ### The runtime bound is `2^{o(n)} · poly(L)` -/\\n\\n/-- An exponent `f` with `2^(f n) = 2^{o(n)}`: `f = o(n)` as `n → ∞`. -/\\ndef IsSubexpExponent (f : ℕ → ℝ) : Prop := f =o[atTop] (fun n : ℕ => (n : ℝ))\\n\\n/-- `runtimeBound C A d L n = C (L + 1)^d 2^(A · runtimeScale n)`, by definition. -/\\ntheorem runtimeBound_eq (C A : ℝ) (d L n : ℕ) :\\n    runtimeBound C A d L n = C * ((L : ℝ) + 1) ^ d * (2 : ℝ) ^ (A * runtimeScale n) := rfl\\n\\n/-- `(log y)² / √y → 0` as `y → ∞`. -/\\ntheorem tendsto_log_sq_div_sqrt :\\n    Tendsto (fun y : ℝ => (Real.log y) ^ 2 / Real.sqrt y) atTop (nhds 0) := by\\n  have h := Real.isLittleO_log_rpow_rpow_atTop (2 : ℝ) (by norm_num : (0 : ℝ) < 1 / 2)\\n  have h' : (fun y : ℝ => (Real.log y) ^ 2) =o[atTop] (fun y : ℝ => Real.sqrt y) := by\\n    refine h.congr' ?_ ?_\\n    · filter_upwards with y\\n      exact Real.rpow_two _\\n    · filter_upwards [eventually_ge_atTop (0 : ℝ)] with y hy\\n      rw [Real.sqrt_eq_rpow]\\n  exact h'.tendsto_div_nhds_zero\\n\\n/-- The verified runtime scale `ρ(n) = n (log log(n + 16))² / √log(n + 16)` is `o(n)`. -/\\ntheorem runtimeScale_isLittleO :\\n    (fun n : ℕ => runtimeScale n) =o[atTop] (fun n : ℕ => (n : ℝ)) := by\\n  have hlog : Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16)) atTop atTop :=\\n    Real.tendsto_log_atTop.comp (tendsto_atTop_add_const_right _ _ tendsto_natCast_atTop_atTop)\\n  have hq : Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => (Real.log (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))) ^ 2 /\\n      Real.sqrt (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))) atTop (nhds 0) :=\\n    tendsto_log_sq_div_sqrt.comp hlog\\n  have h1 : (fun n : ℕ => (Real.log (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))) ^ 2 /\\n      Real.sqrt (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))) =o[atTop] (fun _ : ℕ => (1 : ℝ)) :=\\n    isLittleO_one_iff.mpr hq\\n  have h2 := h1.mul_isBigO (isBigO_refl (fun n : ℕ => (n : ℝ)) atTop)\\n  refine h2.congr' ?_ ?_\\n  · filter_upwards with n\\n    simp only [runtimeScale, Pi.mul_apply]\\n    ring\\n  · filter_upwards with n\\n    simp\\n\\n/-- The verified exponent `A · ρ(n)` is a subexponential exponent, for every `A`. -/\\ntheorem isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale (A : ℝ) :\\n    IsSubexpExponent (fun n : ℕ => A * runtimeScale n) :=\\n  (runtimeScale_isLittleO.const_mul_left A)\\n\\n/-! ### Traces of the located step project to traces of the plain step -/\\n\\ntheorem LocatedCfg.monitor_config {machine : PrimitiveMachine} (c : LocatedCfg machine)\\n    (x : machine.Cfg) : (c.monitor x).config = x := by\\n  unfold LocatedCfg.monitor\\n  rcases hs : c.config.state with b | q\\n  · rfl\\n  · simp only [Sum.elim_inr]\\n    rcases machine.transition q (c.config.tapes (machine.scan q)).head with b' | ⟨q', a⟩\\n    · rfl\\n    · rfl\\n\\n/-- A trace of the located step is a trace of the plain step on the configurations. -/\\ntheorem Trace.config_of_locatedStep {machine : PrimitiveMachine} {t : ℕ}\\n    {c c' : LocatedCfg machine} (h : Trace (locatedStep machine) t c c') :\\n    Trace machine.step t c.config c'.config := by\\n  induction h with\\n  | refl a => exact Trace.refl _\\n  | cons hs _ ih =>\\n    rename_i a b c''\\n    simp only [locatedStep, Option.map_eq_some_iff] at hs\\n    obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := hs\\n    rw [LocatedCfg.monitor_config] at ih\\n    exact Trace.cons hx ih\\n\\n/-! ### The canonical input of a pathwidth decision instance -/\\n\\n/-- The canonical input of the instance `(G, k)`, `G` a graph on `Fin n`: `n` in the\\ncollection's unary code (`encodeNat`), then `k`, then the `n²` adjacency bits row by row. -/\\nnoncomputable def encodeGraph {n : ℕ} (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ) : List Bool :=\\n  open Classical in\\n  Encoding.encodeNat n ++ Encoding.encodeNat k ++\\n    (List.finRange n).flatMap (fun i => (List.finRange n).map (fun j => decide (G.Adj i j)))\\n\\ntheorem encodeGraph_length {n : ℕ} (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ) :\\n    (encodeGraph G k).length = (n + 1) + (k + 1) + n * n := by\\n  simp [encodeGraph, Encoding.encodeNat, List.length_flatMap, List.map_const']\\n\\n/-! ### The subexponential-pathwidth predicates -/\\n\\n/-- A class of graphs, one predicate per vertex count. -/\\nabbrev GraphClass := ∀ n : ℕ, SimpleGraph (Fin n) → Prop\\n\\n/-- `PathwidthSubexpOn C`: some primitive machine decides `pathwidth G ≤ k` for every `G` in\\nthe class `C` and every `k`, on the canonical input, in time `c (L + 1)^d 2^(f n)` with\\n`f = o(n)` in the number of vertices `n`. -/\\ndef PathwidthSubexpOn (C : GraphClass) : Prop :=\\n  ∃ (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (c : ℝ) (d : ℕ) (f : ℕ → ℝ),\\n    0 < c ∧ IsSubexpExponent f ∧\\n    ∀ (n : ℕ) (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ), C n G →\\n      ∃ (time : ℕ) (final : machine.Cfg),\\n        Trace machine.step time (machine.init (encodeGraph G k)) final ∧\\n        final.state = Sum.inl (@decide (pathwidth G ≤ k) (Classical.propDecidable _)) ∧\\n        (time : ℝ) ≤ c * (((encodeGraph G k).length : ℝ) + 1) ^ d * (2 : ℝ) ^ (f n)\\n\\n/-- `PathwidthSubexp`: the same over every graph. -/\\ndef PathwidthSubexp : Prop :=\\n  ∃ (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (c : ℝ) (d : ℕ) (f : ℕ → ℝ),\\n    0 < c ∧ IsSubexpExponent f ∧\\n    ∀ (n : ℕ) (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ),\\n      ∃ (time : ℕ) (final : machine.Cfg),\\n        Trace machine.step time (machine.init (encodeGraph G k)) final ∧\\n        final.state = Sum.inl (@decide (pathwidth G ≤ k) (Classical.propDecidable _)) ∧\\n        (time : ℝ) ≤ c * (((encodeGraph G k).length : ℝ) + 1) ^ d * (2 : ℝ) ^ (f n)\\n\\n/-- Monotonicity in the class: a machine for `C` is a machine for every `C' ⊆ C`. -/\\ntheorem PathwidthSubexpOn.mono {C C' : GraphClass} (h : PathwidthSubexpOn C)\\n    (hsub : ∀ n G, C' n G → C n G) : PathwidthSubexpOn C' := by\\n  obtain ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, hmain⟩ := h\\n  exact ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, fun n G k hG => hmain n G k (hsub n G hG)⟩\\n\\n/-- `PathwidthSubexp` is the class-restricted notion on the class of all graphs. -/\\ntheorem pathwidthSubexp_iff : PathwidthSubexp ↔ PathwidthSubexpOn (fun _ _ => True) := by\\n  constructor\\n  · rintro ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, hmain⟩\\n    exact ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, fun n G k _ => hmain n G k⟩\\n  · rintro ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, hmain⟩\\n    exact ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, fun n G k => hmain n G k trivial⟩\\n\\n/-- The decision bit is the same for vertex separation (Kinnersley). -/\\ntheorem decide_pathwidth_le_eq {n : ℕ} (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ) :\\n    @decide (pathwidth G ≤ k) (Classical.propDecidable _) =\\n      @decide (vertexSeparation G ≤ k) (Classical.propDecidable _) := by\\n  simp only [vertexSeparation_eq_pathwidth]\\n\\n/-- `PathwidthSubexpOn C`, stated with `vertexSeparation` in place of `pathwidth`, for the\\nstatements of item 08 that are made against `VertexSeparation.lean`. -/\\ntheorem pathwidthSubexpOn_iff_vertexSeparation (C : GraphClass) :\\n    PathwidthSubexpOn C ↔\\n    ∃ (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (c : ℝ) (d : ℕ) (f : ℕ → ℝ),\\n      0 < c ∧ IsSubexpExponent f ∧\\n      ∀ (n : ℕ) (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ), C n G →\\n        ∃ (time : ℕ) (final : machine.Cfg),\\n          Trace machine.step time (machine.init (encodeGraph G k)) final ∧\\n          final.state = Sum.inl (@decide (vertexSeparation G ≤ k) (Classical.propDecidable _)) ∧\\n          (time : ℝ) ≤ c * (((encodeGraph G k).length : ℝ) + 1) ^ d * (2 : ℝ) ^ (f n) := by\\n  simp only [PathwidthSubexpOn, decide_pathwidth_le_eq]\\n\\nend MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth\\nEOF\\n(time lake env lean MOSPFormalization/SubexpPathwidth/Frame.lean 2>&1 | head -60) 2>&1\",\"description\":\"Write Frame.lean and type-check it\",\"timeout\":900000},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":32,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":487,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":126413,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":487,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_t