ch by unpacking the existential.","+","+### 2.4 Glue between the two: the verified bound has the target's shape","+","+Two further lemmas, so that a transfer theorem can move from the","+comparator's bound to the target's without analysis of its own:","+","+- `Trace.config_of_locatedStep`: a trace of the located step projects to a","+  trace of the plain step on the underlying configurations","+  (`LocatedCfg.monitor_config : (c.monitor x).config = x`, then induction","+  on the trace). So `SubexpCount`'s `time` is a bound on `machine.step`,","+  the step `PathwidthSubexpOn` uses.","+- `runtimeScale_isLittleO`: `ρ(n) = o(n)`; hence","+  `isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale A : IsSubexpExponent (fun n => A * ρ n)`","+  for every `A`. The analytic content is `tendsto_log_sq_div_sqrt`,","+  `(log y)² / √y → 0`, from Mathlib's `isLittleO_log_rpow_rpow_atTop`","+  (`(log y)^2 = o(y^{1/2})`), composed with `log(n + 16) → ∞`.","+","+With these, `SubexpCount k` already has the form \"a primitive machine","+counts, on canonical CNF input, in time `c (L + 1)^d 2^(f n)` with","+`f = o(n)`\" — the same form as `PathwidthSubexpOn`, with the CNF's","+variable count in place of the vertex count. **That substitution is the","+whole question of the loop**: a transfer needs an encoding whose variable","+count is `o(n √log n / (log log n)²)` (§1.3.8), and §1.3.8's reason that","+no encoding on record comes close stands.","+","+### 2.5 What a transfer theorem will look like, given this frame","+","+For the record, the shape items 08–09 would prove, so that the frame is","+seen to be sufficient. Positive direction (item 09), on a class `C`:","+","+    SubexpCount k →","+    MachineCompose →                                   -- the named composition Prop of §2.1","+    (∃ enc : (n : ℕ) → (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) → ℕ → CNF (Fin (N n G)),","+       (∀ n G k, C n G → WidthAtMost k (enc n G k) ∧ (0 < count (enc n G k) ↔ pathwidth G ≤ k)) ∧","+       (fun n => A · ρ (N n)) = o(n) ∧ ⟨enc computable in polynomial time by a primitive machine⟩) →","+    PathwidthSubexpOn C","+","+The middle hypothesis is the one about pathwidth — the encoding's","+correctness (`sat ↔ pw ≤ k`, checked to 7 vertices before it is stated,","+proved against `VertexSeparation.lean`) and its size — and is where all of","+the loop's mathematics sits. Negative direction (items 07–08), for a","+problem `X` with instances of size `N` and a reduction `red` to pathwidth:","+","+    PathwidthSubexp →","+    MachineCompose →","+    (∀ I, X I ↔ pathwidth (red I) ≤ k I) ∧ (vertices of red I ≤ a · N(I) + b) ∧ ⟨red polynomial-time⟩ →","+    XSubexp","+","+with `XSubexp` defined for `X` in the style of `PathwidthSubexp` when item","+07 fixes `X`. The linearity condition \"vertices `≤ a N + b`\" is what makes","+`f(a N + b) = o(N)` from `f = o(n)`; a quadratic reduction gives","+`f(N²) = o(N²)`, which is nothing (plan §0.4.2).","+","+### 2.6 Checks","+","+- `lake build`: clean, both files imported by `MOSPFormalization.lean`","+  (the gate's import check).","+- Axiom audit: 17 declarations, all `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`","+  (`02_frame/axiom_check.lean`, `.log`).","+- Textual fidelity of the hypothesis: `02_frame/body_diff.log` (identical).","+- Verbatim copy: `diff` empty when made; regenerate per `02_frame/README.md`.","+- No reduction or encoding of pathwidth is stated here, so the brute-force","+  check to 7 vertices has nothing to apply to; `encodeGraph_length` is the","+  one computation and is proved.","+- `python3 Ralph_Loops/loop0014/gate.py`: see PROGRESS.md for the run.","+","+### 2.7 What this does not claim","+","+- That `SubexpCount k` holds for any `k`, or that `ExactCountAndSat` holds:","+  both are `def`s of `Prop`s with no proof and no axiom behind them. That","+  the collection's proof of `exact_count_and_sat` is correct is not","+  examined and not relied on.","+- That `PathwidthSubexp` or any `PathwidthSubexpOn C` holds; nothing here","+  is an algorithm.","+- That the `PrimitiveMachine` model is robust (that it simulates a RAM or","+  a standard multi-tape machine with polynomial overhead): plausible for","+  an ordinary multi-tape Turing machine, not proved, not needed by any","+  statement of this item.","+- That `SubexpCount` restates the *paper's* Theorem 1.1: it restates the","+  verified comparator, whose exponent is weaker (§1.0).","+- That the composition fact of §2.1 holds: it is not yet even stated; item","+  07 or 09 states it as a named `Prop` when first needed.","+- That `encodeGraph` is the input format any later encoding must use; it","+  is the canonical input of the *decision*, and a transfer theorem may","+  compute any other input from it under the composition fact.","+","+### 2.8 Regenerate","+","+    cd lean && lake build","+    lake env lean ../reports/scratch/subexp_pathwidth/02_frame/axiom_check.lean","+    cd .. && cat reports/scratch/subexp_pathwidth/02_frame/README.md   # the two diffs","+    python3 Ralph_Loops/loop0014/gate.py"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/subexp_pathwidth.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019yvj8XtfuKx982mgjg4fuE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
