{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YPVZNJCBANeh7eKgG46CfQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/-\n2\tCopyright (c) 2026 Alexandre Linhares. All rights reserved.\n3\tReleased under the MIT license as described in the file LICENSE.\n4\t\n5\t# The formal frame of loop0014: `SubexpCount`, `PathwidthSubexp`, `PathwidthSubexpOn`\n6\t\n7\tItem 02 of `reports/subexp_pathwidth_plan.md` (§0.4.1, §0.5); `reports/subexp_pathwidth.md` §2.\n8\tEverything the loop proves about a subexponential exact algorithm for pathwidth is stated\n9\tagainst the three `Prop`s of this file:\n10\t\n11\t* `SubexpCount k` — the comparator statement `exact_count_and_sat k` of OpenAI's family 378\n12\t  (*The Exponential Time Hypothesis is False*, 2026-10-25), **restated as a `def` of a `Prop`,\n13\t  never proved and never an axiom**: one fixed primitive multi-tape machine exactly counts the\n14\t  satisfying assignments of every CNF of width `≤ k` on `n` variables, in the collection's\n15\t  canonical encoding of bit length `L`, in time `≤ C (L + 1)^d · 2^(A · ρ(n))` with\n16\t  `ρ(n) = n (log log(n + 16))² / √log(n + 16)`, visiting at most `S (L + 1)^e` tape cells at\n17\t  every step. The body is the comparator's statement character for character (the binder\n18\t  `hk : 2 ≤ k` becomes the hypothesis of `ExactCountAndSat`); the machine model, the encoding\n19\t  and `runtimeBound` are the verbatim copy in `PrimitiveMachine.lean`. This is the *verified*\n20\t  exponent, the weaker one (`reports/subexp_pathwidth.md` §1.0): the paper's\n21\t  `n log log n / √log n` and `n / √log n` are not in the Lean library and are not restated.\n22\t* `PathwidthSubexpOn C` — \"some primitive machine decides `pathwidth G ≤ k` for every graph\n23\t  `G` in the class `C` and every `k`, in time `2^{o(n)} · poly(L)`\": a machine, constants\n24\t  `c > 0`, `d`, and an exponent `f = o(n)` (`Asymptotics.IsLittleO`, so `2^(f n)` is\n25\t  `2^{o(n)}` in the number of vertices), such that on the canonical input `encodeGraph G k`\n26\t  (`n` and `k` in the collection's unary code, then the `n²` adjacency bits) the machine halts\n27\t  in the answer state `decide (pathwidth G ≤ k)` within `c (L + 1)^d 2^(f n)` steps. A class is\n28\t  `GraphClass := ∀ n, SimpleGraph (Fin n) → Prop` (the item's `SimpleGraph → Prop` is not a\n29\t  type; nothing requires the class to be closed under isomorphism).\n30\t* `PathwidthSubexp` — the same over every graph.\n31\t\n32\tThe parameter is the number of vertices `n`, never the input length (`TASK.md`: on dense\n33\tgraphs `L = Θ(n²)`), which is why `f` is `o(n)` and the polynomial factor is in `L`.\n34\t\n35\tThe machine model is the one the counting theorem is stated in, so a transfer theorem\n36\t`SubexpCount k → PathwidthSubexpOn C` (item 09, if any) is a statement about one machine\n37\tmodel and needs no translation between models; the price, recorded in the report, is that\n38\tsuch a theorem needs a composition fact about primitive machines (a polynomial-time encoder\n39\tfollowed by the counting machine), which the comparator does not state and which would be\n40\tcarried as a further named `Prop`. An abstract notion (\"a function with a time function\")\n41\twas rejected because without a cost model `∃ f, ∃ T, …` is provable outright and the\n42\thypothesis would be vacuous.\n43\t\n44\tProved here:\n45\t\n46\t* `SubexpCount.anti`: `SubexpCount k → k' ≤ k → SubexpCount k'` (a width-`≤ k'` formula has\n47\t  width `≤ k`; the same machine and constants).\n48\t* `PathwidthSubexpOn.mono`: a machine for a class is a machine for every subclass.\n49\t* `pathwidthSubexp_iff`: `PathwidthSubexp ↔ PathwidthSubexpOn (fun _ _ => True)`.\n50\t* `pathwidthSubexpOn_iff_vertexSeparation`: the same `Prop` with `vertexSeparation` in place\n51\t  of `pathwidth` (Kinnersley, `vertexSeparation_eq_pathwidth`), for item 08, whose statements\n52\t  are against `VertexSeparation.lean`.\n53\t* `Trace.config_of_locatedStep`: a trace of the located (space-monitoring) step projects to a\n54\t  trace of the plain step, so the time bound of `SubexpCount` is a bound on `machine.step`.\n55\t* `runtimeScale_isLittleO`, `isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale`: the verified exponent\n56\t  `A · ρ(n)` is `o(n)`, so `runtimeBound C A d L n` is of the form `PathwidthSubexpOn` asks\n57\t  for (`runtimeBound_eq`). The analytic content is `(log y)² / √y → 0`.\n58\t\n59\tEvery statement here is a definition or a trivial lemma; nothing was brute-force checked\n60\tbecause nothing is a reduction or an encoding of pathwidth (TASK.md's check applies to those;\n61\t`encodeGraph_length` is the one computation, proved). What this file does **not** claim:\n62\tthat `SubexpCount k` holds for any `k`; that any `PathwidthSubexpOn C` holds; that the\n63\t`PrimitiveMachine` model is robust (polynomially equivalent to any other); or that the\n64\ttheorem of the paper beyond the comparator statement is restated.\n65\t-/\n66\timport MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth.PrimitiveMachine\n67\timport MOSPFormalization.VSEquivPW\n68\t\n69\tset_option linter.unusedSectionVars false\n70\t\n71\tnamespace MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth\n72\t\n73\topen OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT\n74\topen OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation\n75\topen OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace\n76\topen OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement\n77\topen Asymptotics Filter\n78\t\n79\t/-! ### The hypothesis: the comparator statement as a `Prop` -/\n80\t\n81\t/-- **The counting hypothesis, for width `k`**: the body of `exact_count_and_sat k` in\n82\t`lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.lean` of the OpenAI collection, character for\n83\tcharacter. Never proved here, never an axiom. -/\n84\tdef SubexpCount (k : ℕ) : Prop :=\n85\t  ∃ (machine : Computation.PrimitiveMachine)\n86\t    (countTape answerTape : Fin machine.tapeCount)\n87\t    (C A S : ℝ) (d e : ℕ),\n88\t    0 < C ∧ 0 < A ∧ 0 < S ∧ 0 < d ∧ 0 < e ∧\n89\t    ∀ (n : ℕ) (F : SAT.CNF (Fin n)), SAT.WidthAtMost k F →\n90\t      ∃ (time : ℕ) (final : LocatedCfg machine),\n91\t        Computation.Trace (locatedStep machine) time\n92\t          (locatedInit machine (Encoding.encodeCNF F)) final ∧\n93\t        final.config.tapes countTape =\n94\t          Turing.Tape.mk₁ ((countWord (SAT.count F)).map some) ∧\n95\t        final.config.tapes answerTape =\n96\t          Turing.Tape.mk₁ [some (decide (0 < SAT.count F))] ∧\n97\t        final.config.state = Sum.inl (decide (0 < SAT.count F)) ∧\n98\t        BinaryArithmetic.toNat (countWord (SAT.count F)) = SAT.count F ∧\n99\t        (countWord (SAT.count F)).length ≤ n + 1 ∧\n100\t        (time : ℝ) ≤ OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement.runtimeBound C A d\n101\t          (Encoding.formulaBitLength F) n ∧\n102\t        ∀ (prefixSteps : ℕ) (intermediate : LocatedCfg machine),\n103\t          prefixSteps ≤ time →\n104\t          Computation.Trace (locatedStep machine) prefixSteps\n105\t            (locatedInit machine (Encoding.encodeCNF F)) intermediate →\n106\t          (visitedSpace intermediate : ℝ) ≤\n107\t            S * ((Encoding.formulaBitLength F : ℝ) + 1) ^ e\n108\t\n109\t/-- The comparator theorem in full: `SubexpCount k` for every `k ≥ 2`. A `Prop`, not asserted. -/\n110\tdef ExactCountAndSat : Prop := ∀ k : ℕ, 2 ≤ k → SubexpCount k\n111\t\n112\t/-- A machine for width `k` is a machine for every smaller width: `WidthAtMost k' F → WidthAtMost k F`. -/\n113\ttheorem SubexpCount.anti {k k' : ℕ} (h : SubexpCount k) (hk : k' ≤ k) : SubexpCount k' := by\n114\t  obtain ⟨machine, countTape, answerTape, C, A, S, d, e, hC, hA, hS, hd, he, hmain⟩ := h\n115\t  refine ⟨machine, countTape, answerTape, C, A, S, d, e, hC, hA, hS, hd, he, ?_⟩\n116\t  intro n F hF\n117\t  exact hmain n F (fun c hc => le_trans (hF c hc) hk)\n118\t\n119\ttheorem ExactCountAndSat.subexpCount (h : ExactCountAndSat) {k : ℕ} (hk : 2 ≤ k) :\n120\t    SubexpCount k := h k hk\n121\t\n122\t/-! ### The runtime bound is `2^{o(n)} · poly(L)` -/\n123\t\n124\t/-- An exponent `f` with `2^(f n) = 2^{o(n)}`: `f = o(n)` as `n → ∞`. -/\n125\tdef IsSubexpExponent (f : ℕ → ℝ) : Prop := f =o[atTop] (fun n : ℕ => (n : ℝ))\n126\t\n127\t/-- `runtimeBound C A d L n = C (L + 1)^d 2^(A · runtimeScale n)`, by definition. -/\n128\ttheorem runtimeBound_eq (C A : ℝ) (d L n : ℕ) :\n129\t    runtimeBound C A d L n = C * ((L : ℝ) + 1) ^ d * (2 : ℝ) ^ (A * runtimeScale n) := rfl\n130\t\n131\t/-- `(log y)² / √y → 0` as `y → ∞`. -/\n132\ttheorem tendsto_log_sq_div_sqrt :\n133\t    Tendsto (fun y : ℝ => (Real.log y) ^ 2 / Real.sqrt y) atTop (nhds 0) := by\n134\t  have h := isLittleO_log_rpow_rpow_atTop (2 : ℝ) (by norm_num : (0 : ℝ) < 1 / 2)\n135\t  have h' : (fun y : ℝ => (Real.log y) ^ 2) =o[atTop] (fun y : ℝ => Real.sqrt y) := by\n136\t    refine h.congr' ?_ ?_\n137\t    · filter_upwards with y\n138\t      exact Real.rpow_two _\n139\t    · filter_upwards [eventually_ge_atTop (0 : ℝ)] with y hy\n140\t      rw [Real.sqrt_eq_rpow]\n141\t  exact h'.tendsto_div_nhds_zero\n142\t\n143\t/-- The verified runtime scale `ρ(n) = n (log log(n + 16))² / √log(n + 16)` is `o(n)`. -/\n144\ttheorem runtimeScale_isLittleO :\n145\t    (fun n : ℕ => runtimeScale n) =o[atTop] (fun n : ℕ => (n : ℝ)) := by\n146\t  have hlog : Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16)) atTop atTop :=\n147\t    Real.tendsto_log_atTop.comp (tendsto_atTop_add_const_right _ _ tendsto_natCast_atTop_atTop)\n148\t  have hq : Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => (Real.log (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))) ^ 2 /\n149\t      Real.sqrt (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))) atTop (nhds 0) :=\n150\t    tendsto_log_sq_div_sqrt.comp hlog\n151\t  have h1 : (fun n : ℕ => (Real.log (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))) ^ 2 /\n152\t      Real.sqrt (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))) =o[atTop] (fun _ : ℕ => (1 : ℝ)) :=\n153\t    (isLittleO_one_iff ℝ).mpr hq\n154\t  have h2 := h1.mul_isBigO (isBigO_refl (fun n : ℕ => (n : ℝ)) atTop)\n155\t  refine h2.congr' ?_ ?_\n156\t  · filter_upwards with n\n157\t    simp only [runtimeScale]\n158\t    ring\n159\t  · filter_upwards with n\n160\t    simp\n161\t\n162\t/-- The verified exponent `A · ρ(n)` is a subexponential exponent, for every `A`. -/\n163\ttheorem isSubexpExponent_runtimeScale (A : ℝ) :\n164\t    IsSubexpExponent (fun n : ℕ => A * runtimeScale n) :=\n165\t  (runtimeScale_isLittleO.const_mul_left A)\n166\t\n167\t/-! ### Traces of the located step project to traces of the plain step -/\n168\t\n169\ttheorem LocatedCfg.monitor_config {machine : PrimitiveMachine} (c : LocatedCfg machine)\n170\t    (x : machine.Cfg) : (c.monitor x).config = x := by\n171\t  unfold LocatedCfg.monitor\n172\t  rcases hs : c.config.state with b | q\n173\t  · rfl\n174\t  · simp only [Sum.elim_inr]\n175\t    rcases machine.transition q (c.config.tapes (machine.scan q)).head with b' | ⟨q', a⟩\n176\t    · rfl\n177\t    · rfl\n178\t\n179\t/-- A trace of the located step is a trace of the plain step on the configurations. -/\n180\ttheorem Trace.config_of_locatedStep {machine : PrimitiveMachine} {t : ℕ}\n181\t    {c c' : LocatedCfg machine} (h : Trace (locatedStep machine) t c c') :\n182\t    Trace machine.step t c.config c'.config := by\n183\t  induction h with\n184\t  | refl a => exact Trace.refl _\n185\t  | cons hs _ ih =>\n186\t    rename_i a b c''\n187\t    simp only [locatedStep, Option.map_eq_some_iff] at hs\n188\t    obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := hs\n189\t    rw [LocatedCfg.monitor_config] at ih\n190\t    exact Trace.cons hx ih\n191\t\n192\t/-! ### The canonical input of a pathwidth decision instance -/\n193\t\n194\t/-- The canonical input of the instance `(G, k)`, `G` a graph on `Fin n`: `n` in the\n195\tcollection's unary code (`encodeNat`), then `k`, then the `n²` adjacency bits row by row. -/\n196\tnoncomputable def encodeGraph {n : ℕ} (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ) : List Bool :=\n197\t  open Classical in\n198\t  Encoding.encodeNat n ++ Encoding.encodeNat k ++\n199\t    (List.finRange n).flatMap (fun i => (List.finRange n).map (fun j => decide (G.Adj i j)))\n200\t\n201\ttheorem encodeGraph_length {n : ℕ} (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ) :\n202\t    (encodeGraph G k).length = (n + 1) + (k + 1) + n * n := by\n203\t  simp [encodeGraph, Encoding.encodeNat, List.length_flatMap, List.map_const']\n204\t  ring\n205\t\n206\t/-! ### The subexponential-pathwidth predicates -/\n207\t\n208\t/-- A class of graphs, one predicate per vertex count. -/\n209\tabbrev GraphClass := ∀ n : ℕ, SimpleGraph (Fin n) → Prop\n210\t\n211\t/-- `PathwidthSubexpOn C`: some primitive machine decides `pathwidth G ≤ k` for every `G` in\n212\tthe class `C` and every `k`, on the canonical input, in time `c (L + 1)^d 2^(f n)` with\n213\t`f = o(n)` in the number of vertices `n`. -/\n214\tdef PathwidthSubexpOn (C : GraphClass) : Prop :=\n215\t  ∃ (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (c : ℝ) (d : ℕ) (f : ℕ → ℝ),\n216\t    0 < c ∧ IsSubexpExponent f ∧\n217\t    ∀ (n : ℕ) (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ), C n G →\n218\t      ∃ (time : ℕ) (final : machine.Cfg),\n219\t        Trace machine.step time (machine.init (encodeGraph G k)) final ∧\n220\t        final.state = Sum.inl (@decide (pathwidth G ≤ k) (Classical.propDecidable _)) ∧\n221\t        (time : ℝ) ≤ c * (((encodeGraph G k).length : ℝ) + 1) ^ d * (2 : ℝ) ^ (f n)\n222\t\n223\t/-- `PathwidthSubexp`: the same over every graph. -/\n224\tdef PathwidthSubexp : Prop :=\n225\t  ∃ (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (c : ℝ) (d : ℕ) (f : ℕ → ℝ),\n226\t    0 < c ∧ IsSubexpExponent f ∧\n227\t    ∀ (n : ℕ) (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ),\n228\t      ∃ (time : ℕ) (final : machine.Cfg),\n229\t        Trace machine.step time (machine.init (encodeGraph G k)) final ∧\n230\t        final.state = Sum.inl (@decide (pathwidth G ≤ k) (Classical.propDecidable _)) ∧\n231\t        (time : ℝ) ≤ c * (((encodeGraph G k).length : ℝ) + 1) ^ d * (2 : ℝ) ^ (f n)\n232\t\n233\t/-- Monotonicity in the class: a machine for `C` is a machine for every `C' ⊆ C`. -/\n234\ttheorem PathwidthSubexpOn.mono {C C' : GraphClass} (h : PathwidthSubexpOn C)\n235\t    (hsub : ∀ n G, C' n G → C n G) : PathwidthSubexpOn C' := by\n236\t  obtain ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, hmain⟩ := h\n237\t  exact ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, fun n G k hG => hmain n G k (hsub n G hG)⟩\n238\t\n239\t/-- `PathwidthSubexp` is the class-restricted notion on the class of all graphs. -/\n240\ttheorem pathwidthSubexp_iff : PathwidthSubexp ↔ PathwidthSubexpOn (fun _ _ => True) := by\n241\t  constructor\n242\t  · rintro ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, hmain⟩\n243\t    exact ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, fun n G k _ => hmain n G k⟩\n244\t  · rintro ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, hmain⟩\n245\t    exact ⟨machine, c, d, f, hc, hf, fun n G k => hmain n G k trivial⟩\n246\t\n247\topen Classical in\n248\t/-- The decision bit is the same for vertex separation (Kinnersley). -/\n249\ttheorem decide_pathwidth_le_eq {n : ℕ} (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ) :\n250\t    @decide (pathwidth G ≤ k) (Classical.propDecidable _) =\n251\t      @decide (vertexSeparation G ≤ k) (Classical.propDecidable _) :=\n252\t  decide_eq_decide.mpr (by rw [vertexSeparation_eq_pathwidth])\n253\t\n254\topen Classical in\n255\t/-- `PathwidthSubexpOn C`, stated with `vertexSeparation` in place of `pathwidth`, for the\n256\tstatements of item 08 that are made against `VertexSeparation.lean`. -/\n257\ttheorem pathwidthSubexpOn_iff_vertexSeparation (C : GraphClass) :\n258\t    PathwidthSubexpOn C ↔\n259\t    ∃ (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (c : ℝ) (d : ℕ) (f : ℕ → ℝ),\n260\t      0 < c ∧ IsSubexpExponent f ∧\n261\t      ∀ (n : ℕ) (G : SimpleGraph (Fin n)) (k : ℕ), C n G →\n262\t        ∃ (time : ℕ) (final : machine.Cfg),\n263\t          Trace machine.step time (machine.init (encodeGraph G k)) final ∧\n264\t          final.state = Sum.inl (@decide (vertexSeparation G ≤ k) (Classical.propDecidable _)) ∧\n265\t          (time : ℝ) ≤ c * (((encodeGraph G k).length : ℝ) + 1) ^ d * (2 : ℝ) ^ (f n) := by\n266\t  simp only [PathwidthSubexpOn, decide_pathwidth_le_eq]\n267\t\n268\tend MOSPFormalization.SubexpPathwidth\n269\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JBZzBGJ8PbK3yQ8iGYoZD6","agent_id":"a8af74a5bb59c2862","session_id":"0ef12acb-f9ad-4899-992d-6d80c628ee09","uuid":"6c3752f3-846c-4807-856f-868ac40e09dd","timestamp":"2026-11-04T18:52:25.640Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YPVZNJCBANeh7eKgG46CfQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Refuter read of Frame.lean"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Azy77tCJ3n2oLD6ez5uMfk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/-\n2\t# OpenAI's machine model and canonical CNF encoding, copied verbatim\n3\t\n4\tThis file is a **verbatim copy of lines 1–190 and 220** of\n5\t`lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.lean` in the OpenAI mathematics\n6\tcollection (`github.com/openai/math`, commit `4eaee87548250b2682affda7d05d947c05554bae`,\n7\t2026-10-29; the file's SHA-256 is\n8\t`4183b2057cff350d66848215ff7167196dfc20e1891b598fdddea59077a76685`), the comparator\n9\tstatement of family 378, *The Exponential Time Hypothesis is False* (October 25, 2026).\n10\tLines 191–219, the theorem `exact_count_and_sat` with its `sorry`, are **not** copied: its\n11\tstatement is restated as the named `Prop` `SubexpCount` in `Frame.lean`, and it is never\n12\tasserted in this development (loop0014, plan `reports/subexp_pathwidth_plan.md` §0.4.1;\n13\t`reports/subexp_pathwidth.md` §2).\n14\t\n15\tCopyright 2026 OpenAI. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\"); you\n16\tmay not use this file except in compliance with the License. You may obtain a copy of the\n17\tLicense at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0. Unless required by applicable law or\n18\tagreed to in writing, software distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\"\n19\tBASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied. See the\n20\tLicense for the specific language governing permissions and limitations under the License.\n21\tThe copy is recorded in `literature/MISSING.md` (the OpenAI collection entry) and the rest of\n22\tthis development is MIT-licensed as described in the file LICENSE.\n23\t\n24\tNothing below is proved: the file contains definitions only (the canonical encoding of a CNF\n25\tover `Fin n`, the `PrimitiveMachine` multi-tape model over Mathlib's `Turing.TM0.Stmt` and\n26\t`Turing.Tape`, its `Trace`, the located configuration that monitors the visited cells, and the\n27\truntime bound `C (L + 1)^d 2^(A · n (log log(n + 16))² / √log(n + 16))`). The namespaces are\n28\tkept as in the source so that `SubexpCount` reads character for character as the comparator.\n29\tEverything after this comment block is the copy.\n30\t-/\n31\timport Mathlib\n32\t\n33\tnamespace OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.BinaryArithmetic\n34\t\n35\tdef bitVal (b : Bool) : ℕ := if b then 1 else 0\n36\t\n37\tdef toNat : List Bool → ℕ\n38\t  | [] => 0\n39\t  | b :: bs => bitVal b + 2 * toNat bs\n40\t\n41\tend OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.BinaryArithmetic\n42\t\n43\tnamespace OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SAT\n44\t\n45\tuniverse u\n46\t\n47\tabbrev Assignment (V : Type u) := V → Bool\n48\t\n49\tstructure Literal (V : Type u) where\n50\t  «variable» : V\n51\t  positive : Bool\n52\t  deriving DecidableEq\n53\t\n54\tabbrev Clause (V : Type u) := Finset (Literal V)\n55\tabbrev CNF (V : Type u) := Finset (Clause V)\n56\t\n57\tvariable {V : Type u} [DecidableEq V]\n58\t\n59\tdef Literal.eval (a : Assignment V) (l : Literal V) : Bool :=\n60\t  a l.variable == l.positive\n61\t\n62\tdef Clause.eval (a : Assignment V) (C : Clause V) : Bool :=\n63\t  decide (∃ l ∈ C, l.eval a = true)\n64\t\n65\tdef CNF.eval (a : Assignment V) (F : CNF V) : Bool :=\n66\t  decide (∀ C ∈ F, C.eval a = true)\n67\t\n68\tdef WidthAtMost (k : ℕ) (F : CNF V) : Prop := ∀ C ∈ F, C.card ≤ k\n69\t\n70\tsection Finite\n71\t\n72\tvariable [Fintype V]\n73\t\n74\tdef satisfyingAssignments (F : CNF V) : Finset (Assignment V) :=\n75\t  Finset.univ.filter fun a => F.eval a = true\n76\t\n77\tdef count (F : CNF V) : ℕ := (satisfyingAssignments F).card\n78\t\n79\tend Finite\n80\t\n81\tend OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SAT\n82\t\n83\tnamespace OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Encoding\n84\t\n85\tdef encodeNat (n : ℕ) : List Bool := List.replicate n true ++ [false]\n86\t\n87\tdef frame (bits : List Bool) : List Bool :=\n88\t  bits.foldr (fun b rest => true :: b :: rest) [false]\n89\t\n90\tdef encodeList {α : Type*} (enc : α → List Bool) : List α → List Bool\n91\t  | [] => [false]\n92\t  | a :: as => true :: (frame (enc a) ++ encodeList enc as)\n93\t\n94\tdef literalCode {n : ℕ} (l : SAT.Literal (Fin n)) : ℕ :=\n95\t  2 * l.variable.val + if l.positive then 1 else 0\n96\t\n97\tdef clauseNumbers {n : ℕ} (C : SAT.Clause (Fin n)) : List ℕ :=\n98\t  (C.image literalCode).sort (· ≤ ·)\n99\t\n100\tdef cnfNumbers {n : ℕ} (F : SAT.CNF (Fin n)) : List (List ℕ) :=\n101\t  (F.image clauseNumbers).sort (· ≤ ·)\n102\t\n103\tdef encodeCNFBody {n : ℕ} (F : SAT.CNF (Fin n)) : List Bool :=\n104\t  encodeList (encodeList encodeNat) (cnfNumbers F)\n105\t\n106\tdef encodeCNF {n : ℕ} (F : SAT.CNF (Fin n)) : List Bool :=\n107\t  encodeNat n ++ encodeCNFBody F\n108\t\n109\tdef formulaBitLength {n : ℕ} (F : SAT.CNF (Fin n)) : ℕ := (encodeCNF F).length\n110\t\n111\tend OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Encoding\n112\t\n113\tnamespace OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation\n114\t\n115\tuniverse u\n116\t\n117\tinductive Trace {α : Type u} (step : α → Option α) : ℕ → α → α → Prop\n118\t  | refl (a : α) : Trace step 0 a a\n119\t  | cons {n : ℕ} {a b c : α} :\n120\t      step a = some b → Trace step n b c → Trace step (n + 1) a c\n121\t\n122\tstructure PrimitiveMachine where\n123\t  tapeCount : ℕ\n124\t  stateCount : ℕ\n125\t  inputTape : Fin tapeCount\n126\t  start : Fin stateCount\n127\t  scan : Fin stateCount → Fin tapeCount\n128\t  transition : Fin stateCount → Option Bool →\n129\t    Bool ⊕ (Fin stateCount × Turing.TM0.Stmt (Option Bool))\n130\t\n131\tnamespace PrimitiveMachine\n132\t\n133\tstructure Cfg (machine : PrimitiveMachine) where\n134\t  state : Bool ⊕ Fin machine.stateCount\n135\t  tapes : Fin machine.tapeCount → Turing.Tape (Option Bool)\n136\t\n137\tdef step (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (c : machine.Cfg) : Option machine.Cfg :=\n138\t  match c.state with\n139\t  | .inl _ => none\n140\t  | .inr q =>\n141\t    let tapeIndex := machine.scan q\n142\t    match machine.transition q (c.tapes tapeIndex).head with\n143\t    | .inl answer => some ⟨.inl answer, c.tapes⟩\n144\t    | .inr (q', action) =>\n145\t      let nextTape :=\n146\t        match action with\n147\t        | .move direction => (c.tapes tapeIndex).move direction\n148\t        | .write symbol => (c.tapes tapeIndex).write symbol\n149\t      some ⟨.inr q', Function.update c.tapes tapeIndex nextTape⟩\n150\t\n151\tdef init (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (input : List Bool) : machine.Cfg :=\n152\t  ⟨.inr machine.start, fun k =>\n153\t    if k = machine.inputTape then Turing.Tape.mk₁ (input.map some)\n154\t    else Turing.Tape.mk₁ []⟩\n155\t\n156\tend PrimitiveMachine\n157\t\n158\tend OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation\n159\t\n160\tnamespace OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement\n161\t\n162\tnoncomputable def runtimeScale (n : ℕ) : ℝ :=\n163\t  (n : ℝ) * (Real.log (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))) ^ 2 /\n164\t    Real.sqrt (Real.log ((n : ℝ) + 16))\n165\t\n166\tnoncomputable def runtimeBound (constant exponentConstant : ℝ)\n167\t    (degree inputBits numVars : ℕ) : ℝ :=\n168\t  constant * ((inputBits : ℝ) + 1) ^ degree *\n169\t    (2 : ℝ) ^ (exponentConstant * runtimeScale numVars)\n170\t\n171\tend OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLog.Statement\n172\t\n173\tnamespace OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace\n174\t\n175\topen OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Computation\n176\t\n177\tdef countWord (a : ℕ) : List Bool := if a = 0 then [false] else a.bits\n178\t\n179\tstructure LocatedCfg (machine : PrimitiveMachine) where\n180\t  config : machine.Cfg\n181\t  position : Fin machine.tapeCount → ℤ\n182\t  lower : Fin machine.tapeCount → ℤ\n183\t  upper : Fin machine.tapeCount → ℤ\n184\t\n185\tdef locatedInit (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (input : List Bool) : LocatedCfg machine where\n186\t  config := machine.init input\n187\t  position _ := 0\n188\t  lower _ := 0\n189\t  upper i := if i = machine.inputTape then Int.ofNat (input.length - 1) else 0\n190\t\n191\tdef headDisplacement : Turing.TM0.Stmt (Option Bool) → ℤ\n192\t  | .move .left => -1\n193\t  | .move .right => 1\n194\t  | .write _ => 0\n195\t\n196\tdef LocatedCfg.monitor {machine : PrimitiveMachine} (c : LocatedCfg machine)\n197\t    (config : machine.Cfg) : LocatedCfg machine :=\n198\t  Sum.elim\n199\t    (fun _ => { c with config })\n200\t    (fun q =>\n201\t      Sum.elim\n202\t        (fun _ => { c with config })\n203\t        (fun targetAction =>\n204\t          let action := targetAction.2\n205\t          let i := machine.scan q\n206\t          let position := c.position i + headDisplacement action\n207\t          { config\n208\t            position := Function.update c.position i position\n209\t            lower := Function.update c.lower i (min (c.lower i) position)\n210\t            upper := Function.update c.upper i (max (c.upper i) position) })\n211\t        (machine.transition q (c.config.tapes (machine.scan q)).head))\n212\t    c.config.state\n213\t\n214\tdef locatedStep (machine : PrimitiveMachine) (c : LocatedCfg machine) :\n215\t    Option (LocatedCfg machine) :=\n216\t  (machine.step c.config).map c.monitor\n217\t\n218\tdef visitedSpace {machine : PrimitiveMachine} (c : LocatedCfg machine) : ℕ :=\n219\t  ∑ i, (c.upper i - c.lower i + 1).toNat\n220\t\n221\tend OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace\n222\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JBZzBGJ8PbK3yQ8iGYoZD6","agent_id":"a8af74a5bb59c2862","session_id":"0ef12acb-f9ad-4899-992d-6d80c628ee09","uuid":"05fd92e1-1055-4bc0-ae8d-ac3d33e9a58d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T18:52:25.642Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Azy77tCJ3n2oLD6ez5uMfk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Refuter read of Frame.lean"}
