{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgiPwnmduaXzKkiJiuvxh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Findings (lines refer to `Frame.lean`; checks run in a scratch file against the built library, nothing edited).\n\n1. **Not vacuous, not trivially refutable** (ll. 214–231). Zero-step loophole closed: `Trace.refl` forces `final = machine.init …`, whose state is `.inr machine.start` (PrimitiveMachine.lean l. 152), never `Sum.inl _` — I proved `¬ (m.init inp).state = Sum.inl b` in Lean. Negative `f`, `d = 0`, tiny `c` only tighten the bound (the Prop is existential, so they help neither a proof nor a refutation); `f` is quantified before `n, G, k`, so it is uniform. `init` places the input on `inputTape` via `Tape.mk₁`, head on the first bit, other tapes blank (`none`); readable. The `k` parameter is unbounded, but the machine may answer `true` once it has read `n + 1` ones of `k`, so no obstacle. `Classical.propDecidable` is harmless: any two `Decidable` instances give the same `decide` (checked). Expected degeneracies only: `PathwidthSubexpOn (fun _ _ => False)` is provable (I built the one-state machine), and finite classes are provable by lookup — correct behaviour, not a flaw.\n\n2. **`IsSubexpExponent` is the standard `2^{o(n)}`** (l. 125). Mathlib's `IsLittleO` on `ℕ → ℝ` says `∀ ε > 0, eventually |f n| ≤ ε n`: `(log n)^c` allowed, `εn` excluded, constants allowed (so P-time is included, as it should be). One referee remark: this is the *single-machine* form; Impagliazzo–Paturi's `¬ETH` is `∀ ε ∃ machine in 2^{εn}`. Since the source hypothesis is also single-machine, the transfer direction is consistent — say so once in the report.\n\n3. **`SubexpCount` matches** (ll. 84–107). `#print SubexpCount` with `pp.fullNames` resolves every name to `OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.*`, none to Mathlib's root `Computation` or `Encoding` (no root `Encoding.encodeNat` exists). I could not diff against the untrusted clone myself; `02_frame/body_diff.log` records 23 identical lines, and the printed term is consistent with it.\n\n4. **`encodeGraph` is well-formed** (ll. 196–204): `encodeNat n ++ encodeNat k ++ n²` row-major bits, each unary block self-delimiting, so decodable. Length `(n+1)+(k+1)+n·n` is right. Redundancy (symmetric, zero diagonal) is harmless.\n\n5. **Minor referee points, statements only.** (a) `L` contains `k`, so the polynomial factor is `poly(n² + k)`, not `poly(n)`; harmless (trivial for `k ≥ n`), but a sentence saying so, or restricting to `k < n`, would pre-empt the objection. (b) `0 < d` in `SubexpCount` vs unconstrained `d` in `PathwidthSubexpOn`: harmless, `d = 0 ⊂ d = 1`. (c) The graph is labelled (`SimpleGraph (Fin n)`), so the machine is required to be correct on every labelling — stronger than isomorphism-invariant, fine as a hypothesis target. (d) No space bound in `PathwidthSubexpOn`, which is the right (weaker) conclusion form.\n\nNo concrete problem found."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3156,"cache_read_input_tokens":88200,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3156,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JBZzBGJ8PbK3yQ8iGYoZD6","agent_id":"a8af74a5bb59c2862","session_id":"0ef12acb-f9ad-4899-992d-6d80c628ee09","uuid":"40cccb52-baa1-4f00-accf-13659986e748","timestamp":"2026-11-04T18:55:42.243Z","request_id":"req_011CgiPwnLqMge4fKEioD9Ew","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Refuter read of Frame.lean"}
